# Day 25 - GitHub Pages and Live Website

## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned what GitHub Pages is.
* Learned how websites can be hosted for free.
* Learned how to share a live website.

## GitHub Pages

GitHub Pages is a free hosting service provided by GitHub.

It allows static websites to be published directly from a repository.

## Website Deployment Flow

VS Code
↓
GitHub Repository
↓
GitHub Pages
↓
Live Website

## Practical Work

* Opened GitHub Pages settings.
* Located the live website URL.
* Added the live website link to README.md.

## Key Takeaways

* GitHub Pages provides free hosting.
* A repository can be converted into a live website.
* README files should include a live demo link.
